From: Devon Openheim <devopenm@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 17:28:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] [RFC v1 1/2] dt-bindings: arm: asr: add ASR1802S SoC +
 Ooredoo R291 v2 board
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add YAML device-tree bindings for the ASR ASR1802S (KAGU) SoC and the
Ooredoo R291 v2 reference board.  All MMIO / IRQ / flash‑partition data is
runtime-extracted from a shipping unit (vendor kernel 3.10.33) and
documented inline under 'description'.

The SoC has no mainline support today; these bindings are RFC to seed the
upcoming SoC‑port series (clock/reset/pinctrl/irq/SPI‑NAND/PCIe/eth).

Extracted with root shell (paramiko) + U‑Boot env (mtd21) + bit‑exact
rootfs-a.bin/kernel-a.bin backups in ooredoo_backup/probe.
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/arm/asr/asr1802s.yaml | 91 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../bindings/arm/asr/ooredoo-r291-v2.yaml     | 53 +++++++++++
 2 files changed, 144 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/asr/asr1802s.yaml
 create mode 100644 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/asr/ooredoo-r291-v2.yaml

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/asr/asr1802s.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/asr/asr1802s.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..39fd524
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/asr/asr1802s.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,91 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0 OR BSD-2-Clause)
+#
+# Device Tree binding for the ASR Microelectronics ASR1802S SoC.
+# ASR1802S is an ARM Cortex-A9 (ARMv7-A) communication/IAD SoC sold in
+# Ooredoo R291 v2 gateways (board code "KAGU").  Nothing in this SoC is
+# supported by mainline Linux today; this binding is RFC material for an
+# upstream "SoC support" series (clock/reset/pinctrl/irq/DDR) which must
+# land before the board can boot a mainline kernel.
+#
+# All MMIO / IRQ / partition data below was extracted at runtime from a
+# shipping unit (kernel 3.10.33 vendor, /proc/iomem, /proc/interrupts,
+# /proc/mtd and U-Boot env on mtd21).  Addresses are physical.
+title: ASR ASR1802S SoC (KAGU)
+
+maintainer: Devon Openheim <devopenm@proton.me>
+
+description:
+  ASR1802S SoC.  Single Cortex-A9 (arch_id 0xc07) core, 128 MiB system
+  RAM (32 MiB of which is permanently reserved for the Communication
+  Processor, cpmem=32M@0x6000000), SPI-NAND attached to an on-SoC QSPI
+  controller, dual Gen1×1 PCIe host ports (used here by two Realtek
+  RTL8812FE PCI-e WiFi chips), an integrated Ethernet MAC, a 88PM802
+  PMIC on I2C, a MAX1919/SLIC VoIP front-end, USB3 (DWC3) and an MMC
+  host.  The SoC is booted by a Marvell-derived U-Boot with bootcmd
+  "mrvlboot".
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    description:
+      Should be the SoC: "asr,1802s".  Board-level compatible strings
+      ("asr,1802s-evb") may be listed ahead of the SoC string.
+    const: asr,1802s
+
+  "#address-cells":
+    description: 1 cells for 32-bit MMIO space used by the APB/AXI buses.
+    enum: [1, 2]
+  "#size-cells":
+    enum: [1, 2]
+  "#interrupt-cells":
+    description: IRQs are wired to the ASR ICU interrupt controller.
+    const: 3
+
+  soc:
+    type: object
+    description: Root of the SoC register space.  Buses:
+      - APB  at 0xd4000000 (UART/RTC/SPI/I2C/thermal/pinctrl)
+      - AXI  at 0xd4200000 (PCIe PHYs, MMC, Ethernet, QSPI, USB3)
+      - PCIe MMIO aperture 0xd8200000 (wlan0) and 0xe0100000 (wlan1)
+    properties:
+      compatible:
+        const: simple-bus
+      ranges:
+        description: MMIO windows decoded by the SoC address space.
+
+  memory:
+    description: 128 MiB of system RAM at 0x0.  The lower 32 MiB at
+      0x06000000..0x08000000 is reserved for the CP.
+    reg:
+      maxItems: 1
+
+  "#cpus":
+    description: Single Cortex-A9 core.
+    const: 1
+
+  cpus:
+    type: object
+
+  chosen:
+    properties:
+      stdout-path:
+        description: Primary UART for the serial console.
+        const: serial0
+
+  reserved-memory:
+    description: 32 MiB CP carve-out (cpmem=32M@0x6000000).
+    properties:
+      "#address-cells": [1, 2]
+      "#size-cells": [1, 1]
+
+additionalProperties: true
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    // Minimal SoC + KAGU board.  Peripheral offsets are taken from the
+    // runtime probe in ooredoo_backup/probe/*.
+    #include "asr1826s-kagu.dts"
+    / {
+            model = "Ooredoo R291 v2 (ASR 1826s / KAGU)";
+            compatible = "asr,1802s-evb", "asr,1802s";
+            soc { compatible = "simple-bus"; #address-cells = <1>; #size-cells = <1>; };
+    };
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/asr/ooredoo-r291-v2.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/asr/ooredoo-r291-v2.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f00b734
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/asr/ooredoo-r291-v2.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0 OR BSD-2-Clause)
+title: Ooredoo R291 v2 (ASR 1826s / KAGU)
+
+maintainer: Devon Openheim <devopenm@proton.me>
+
+description:
+  Ooredoo R291 v2 IAD gateway built on the ASR Microelectronics ASR1802S
+  SoC (single Cortex-A9, 128 MiB RAM).  The board is referred to as
+  "KAGU" / "ASR 1826s (KAGU) Board EVB" in the vendor device tree and
+  U-Boot bootargs.
+
+  Hardware summary (extracted from the running unit, kernel 3.10.33):
+    - SoC            : ASR1802S (compatible "asr,1802s-evb","asr,1802s")
+    - CPU            : ARMv7-Cortex-A9 @ ~1 GHz
+    - Flash          : 128 MiB SPI-NAND (F35UQA001G, 128 KiB erase) A/B dual-bank + UBI overlay
+    - RAM            : 128 MiB (32 MiB reserved for the CP)
+    - Console        : ttyS0 @ 115200n8 (pxa2xx-uart, MMIO 0xd4017000, irq 59)
+    - WiFi           : 2x Realtek RTL8812FE on PCIe gen1x1 (vendor driver rtl8192cd.ko)
+    - Ethernet       : ASR MAC @ 0xd4281800 (irq 42/43) + YT9215 switch
+    - USB3           : DWC3 (irq 76) + ASR USB3 PHY @ c0030000
+    - MMC            : mmc0 @ 0xd4280000 (irq 71)
+    - PMIC           : 88PM802 on I2C@0x30 (d4037000, irq 12089)
+    - VoIP           : MAX1919/SLIC (GPIO23 reset, GPIO24 wakeup) — 2 FXS
+    - U-Boot         : Marvell "mrvlboot", bootdelay=1, verify=no, loadaddr=0x8000
+
+  NOTE: WiFi is served by the proprietary rtl8192cd (binary-only, kernel 3.10).
+  The in-tree rtw88 driver supports RTL8812FE as of Linux 5.13+ and is the
+  intended replacement; until the SoC port lands, WiFi must remain on the
+  vendor kernel fork.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    description: Root compatible must include the SoC strings exposed by the
+      shipped device tree so the DTB matches the running hardware.
+    oneOf:
+      - items:
+          - const: asr,1802s-evb
+          - const: asr,1802s
+    deprecated:
+      - description: "ooredoo,r291-v2"   # alias for future machine matching
+
+  soc:
+    description: "KAGU board peripherals are sub-nodes of the ASR1802S SoC."
+    $ref: /schemas/soc/asr/asr1802s.yaml#
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+
+unevaluatedProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    #include "asr1826s-kagu.dts"
